  "configuration_id": "config_008",
  "reason": "Evidence: All four completed experiments used scgpt as the RNA encoder, with config_020 (scgpt + imagenet_vit_l + avgpool + weighted) achieving the best accuracy at 0.542. We have no evidence about how other RNA encoders perform with this best image/fusion/aggregation setup. Question: config_008 (scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + avgpool + weighted) isolates the RNA encoder choice while holding the three best-performing hyperparameters fixed. This tests whether a lighter, learned nonlinear encoder (scvi_n200) can match or exceed scgpt, or whether scgpt's pretrained biological knowledge is essential. Why this is the best next step: With 5 experiments remaining, confirming or refuting the RNA encoder's contribution is the highest-uncertainty question. If scvi_n200 matches scgpt, we unlock cheaper future experiments; if it falls short, we confirm scgpt is the right choice and can focus remaining budget on other axes. Expected cost: scvi_n200 is a compact 200-dim VAE, significantly lighter than scgpt, so this should train in roughly 2–2.5 GPU hours—cheaper than config_020's 2.94 hours while using the same imagenet_vit_l backbone."
}

